@startuml pattern-state
!include style.iuml
' State pattern: what an incident may do depends on its status, and each status is a class.
' The hidden links only arrange the nine state classes in reading order, three per row.
set separator none
hide empty members
skinparam nodesep 16
skinparam ranksep 34

class Incident {
  - status : Status
  + getState() : IncidentState
  + transitionTo(target)
}
interface IncidentState {
  + transitions() : List<Transition>
  + canTransitionTo(target) : boolean
  + onEnter(incident, from, now)
  + onExit(incident, to, now)
  + allowsRating() : boolean
}
class Transition <<record>> {
  target : Status
  labels : Map<Role, String>
  noteRequired : boolean
}
class NewState
class ClassifiedState
class AssignedState
class AcknowledgedState
class InProgressState
class AwaitingInfoState {
  + onEnter() : pause SLA clock
  + onExit() : resume it
}
class ResolvedState
class VerifiedState
class ClosedState {
  + transitions() : none
}
Incident .right.> IncidentState : delegates to the\nstate of its status
IncidentState .right.> Transition
IncidentState <|.. NewState
IncidentState <|.. ClassifiedState
IncidentState <|.. AssignedState
IncidentState <|.. AcknowledgedState
IncidentState <|.. InProgressState
IncidentState <|.. AwaitingInfoState
IncidentState <|.. ResolvedState
IncidentState <|.. VerifiedState
IncidentState <|.. ClosedState
NewState -[hidden]down- AcknowledgedState
ClassifiedState -[hidden]down- InProgressState
AssignedState -[hidden]down- AwaitingInfoState
AcknowledgedState -[hidden]down- ResolvedState
InProgressState -[hidden]down- VerifiedState
AwaitingInfoState -[hidden]down- ClosedState
@enduml
